# Machine-written dormancy state, not configuration. Every sweep rewrites it,
# so committing it would put a churning file with 543 strike counts in front of
# every review, and a merge conflict in it would be resolved by guessing. The
# history worth keeping is in the run graphs: they publish which endpoints were
# skipped and why, run by run, and the state file is only ever the latest view
# of what those runs already recorded.
#
# `dormancy init` creates it, `dormancy` and the sweep write it. A deployment
# that needs it to survive a restart mounts this directory.
state/
